Z||000000||Haze_Performance||07-04-2000||01:31 PM||||I like the idea of dash gauges on a Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/scgaug.jpg">  But I still want the heater & A/C vents. (Like in the Mustang pic below)<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mustangcage.jpg"> <P>Im working on a new dash panel that still has 1/2 of the vents on each side. Ill keep you posted,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Carl (85 Fiero) My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>Haze Mustang Performance</A>   &  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A>||||reg||7
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||07-04-2000||02:02 PM||||Why not try and use the Mustang gauge pods, if the whole panel is going to be replaced like in the first pic (whose is that anyway?  Looks cool) then it shouldn't matter if the total size is bigger. (the mustang vents look  like they are about as wide as the radio) if the back part can be made to fit the original vent holes. <BR>If not, how about 1 vent in between the 2 gauges? It could be split to divert air to both sides of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||07-04-2000||06:38 PM||||I was looking at my vents again and I think that the mustang one might work. But if it doesn't, there are those small vents by the doors under the bigger ones that you could use. You could also redo the rally gauges so there is four round ones instead of the two rectangular ones. My oil gauge doesn't work right anyway.<P>Just my $1.75<BR>Hope it helps or at least doesn't hurt.||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||07-04-2000||07:00 PM||||you know those cups people put guages on the hood of their car in? what about one or two of those mounted to the left or right side of your main instrument pod? i have a cobbled up one on the right side (sitting in the seat) of mine. it was kind of a "hmmm, wonder if" thing so i don't have anything in it yet. i mean to put my volt meter in it.<P>i guess i should mention the "hmmm, what if " thing sometimes can't be reversed, but since it's my car i don't have to answer to anyone. follow at your own risk.<p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 07-04-2000).]||||reg||1
